<title>UK: UK oil stocks dip as investors take profits.</title>
<headline>UK oil stocks dip as investors take profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK oil stocks weakened in afternoon trading as profit-taking sent shares lower after the sector's recent run, traders said.</p>
<p>Shares in Enterprise Oil led the sector lower, dropping 13-1/2p to 571-1/2p. BP fell 8p to 691-1/2p and Burmah Castrol 10-1/2p to 1,126p.</p>
<p>Shell Transport &amp; Trading, which recently hit record highs after news that it was in talks with Texaco over a possible merger of its downstream operations, slipped 9-1/2p to 1,030-1/2p.</p>
<p>&quot;The stocks have done remarkably well recently. We're really just seeing some cashing in of profits,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
